# Line-ending rules for dsh-keepup.
#
# Why this file exists: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default)
# and no .gitattributes, Git rewrites these files to LF on commit, which
# silently breaks the launcher:
#
#   - cmd.exe needs CRLF in .cmd files; goto labels and multi-line blocks can
#     misparse on LF
#   - dsh-keepup.ps1 must keep its UTF-8 BOM, because Windows PowerShell 5.1
#     reads a BOM-less script as ANSI/GBK and turns the Chinese text into
#     mojibake or a parse error
#
# Every rule below is explicit: no catch-all, so no attribute conflicts. Files
# are stored with LF in the repository and checked out with the eol named here.

# cmd.exe requires CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

# Windows PowerShell. eol=crlf also preserves the BOM: Git keeps the leading
# bytes of a text file, so the UTF-8 BOM round-trips intact.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf

# Source, docs and config: LF everywhere.
*.md text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never diff, never convert.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
